Vikram and Betal: The Brave Boy

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a young boy who was very brave,” said Betal. “He lived in a small village.”

One day, a wild animal entered the village and scared everyone.

The villagers ran away and hid in their homes.

But the brave boy stepped forward.

He did not have any weapons, but he used his intelligence.

He made loud noises and lit a fire to scare the animal away.

The animal got frightened and ran back into the forest.

The villagers came out and praised the boy.

Later, the king heard about his bravery and rewarded him.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the boy truly brave?”

Vikram replied, “True bravery is not about strength, but about courage and smart thinking.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Bravery comes from courage and intelligence.
